      "widgets_values": [
        "\n\n# ❄️ IceKiub's Musubi Tuner - ComfyUI Custom Nodes\n\n**Created by IceKiub** | [Support on Patreon](https://patreon.com/IceKiub?utm_medium=unknown&utm_source=join_link&utm_campaign=creatorshare_creator&utm_content=copyLink)\n\n## 📦 Installation\n\n### Quick Install (Recommended)\n\n1. **Download** this `comfyui_nodes` folder to your ComfyUI custom_nodes:\n   ```bash\n   cd ComfyUI/custom_nodes\n   # Download or copy the comfyui_nodes folder here\n   # Rename it to something like: musubi_tuner\n   ```\n\n2. **Run the installer** to setup musubi-tuner dependencies:\n   \n   **Windows:**\n   ```cmd\n   cd musubi_tuner\n   install.bat\n   ```\n   \n   **Linux/Mac:**\n   ```bash\n   cd musubi_tuner\n   python install.py\n   ```\n   \n   The installer will:\n   - ✅ Check for existing musubi-tuner installation\n   - ✅ Optionally clone musubi-tuner from: https://github.com/kohya-ss/musubi-tuner.git\n   - ✅ Verify requirements and guide you through setup\n\n3. **Restart ComfyUI**\n\n### Method 1: Copy to ComfyUI custom_nodes\n1. Copy the entire musubi-tuner folder to ComfyUI:\n   ```bash\n   cp -r Z:/path/musubi-tuner \"C:/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/musubi-tuner\"\n   ```\n2. Restart ComfyUI\n3. Nodes will auto-detect the installation path\n\n### Method 3: Separate Installation with Path Configuration\nIf you keep musubi-tuner separate from ComfyUI:\n\n1. Copy only the `comfyui_nodes` folder to ComfyUI:\n   ```bash\n   cp -r musubi-tuner/comfyui_nodes \"C:/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/ComfyUI_IceKiub_Musubi\"\n   ```\n\n2. In each node, specify `musubi_tuner_path`:\n   ```\n   Z:/vidtraiing/MoUsou/musubi-tuner\n   ```\n\n3. The nodes will remember this path for future use\n\n\nIf auto-detection fails, manually specify `musubi_tuner_path` in the node.\n\n## 🎯 Available Nodes\n\n### 1. ❄️ Musubi Dataset Config\n**Purpose**: Create and configure dataset settings for training\n\n**Inputs**:\n- `config_type`: Choose between WAN Video, QWEN Image, Load from File, or Custom\n- `resolution_width/height`: Target resolution for training data\n- `caption_extension`: File extension for captions (.txt, .caption, .json)\n- `batch_size`: Batch size for training (default: 2)\n- `enable_bucket`: Allow different aspect ratios\n- `bucket_no_upscale`: Don't upscale images smaller than resolution\n- `load_from_file`: Path to existing dataset_config.toml to load\n- `dataset_1/2/3_image_dir`: Paths to your training data (supports up to 3 datasets)\n- `dataset_1/2/3_cache_dir`: Cache directories for each dataset\n- `dataset_1/2/3_num_repeats`: How many times to repeat each dataset\n- `num_frames`: (Video only) Number of frames to use\n- `frame_extraction`: (Video only) head, tail, or uniform\n- `output_path`: Where to save the config file\n\n**Outputs**:\n- `config_path`: Path to the generated config file\n- `config_content`: Preview of the TOML content\n\n**Features**:\n- **Load from File**: Select \"Load from File\" mode and specify existing config path\n- **Multiple Datasets**: Configure up to 3 different datasets in one config\n- **Auto-formatting**: Uses proper TOML format with toml library\n- **Cache Directories**: Specify separate cache folders for each dataset\n\n**Usage**: \n- To create new config: Set paths for dataset_1, optionally dataset_2 and dataset_3\n- To load existing: Set config_type to \"Load from File\", specify path in load_from_file\n- Example template provided: `comfyui_nodes/dataset_config_template.toml`\n\n### 2. ❄️ Musubi Cache (Latents & Text)\n**Purpose**: Pre-cache latents and text embeddings for faster training\n\n**Inputs**:\n- `model_type`: WAN 2.2 or QWEN Image\n- `dataset_config`: Path from Dataset Config node\n- `vae_path`: Path to VAE model\n- `t5_path`: Path to T5 text encoder\n- `cache_latents`: Whether to cache latents\n- `cache_text_encoder`: Whether to cache text embeddings\n- `text_batch_size`: Batch size for text encoding\n- `musubi_tuner_path`: (Optional) Path to musubi-tuner installation\n- `execute`: Set to True to run the caching\n\n**Outputs**:\n- `status`: Current status message\n- `log`: Detailed execution log\n\n**Usage**: Run this after creating your dataset config and before training. Caching speeds up training significantly. If you get \"Script not found\" errors, specify the `musubi_tuner_path`.\n\n### 3. ❄️ Musubi Training\n**Purpose**: Train LoRA networks with full parameter control\n\n**Inputs**:\n- `model_type`: WAN 2.2 or QWEN Image\n- `task`: Training task (t2v-A14B, t2v-B14B, i2v-A14B, i2v-B14B)\n- `dataset_config`: Path to config file\n- `vae_path`, `t5_path`, `dit_path`: Model paths\n- `output_dir`: Where to save the trained LoRA\n- `output_name`: Name for the LoRA file\n- `learning_rate`: Learning rate (default: 0.0003)\n- `network_dim`: LoRA rank (default: 32)\n- `network_alpha`: LoRA alpha (default: 32)\n- `max_train_steps`: Total training steps\n- `save_every_n_steps`: Checkpoint frequency\n- `use_high_noise`: Enable high noise training (WAN only)\n- `dit_high_noise_path`: Path to high noise model\n- `timestep_boundary`: Timestep boundary for high noise\n- `musubi_tuner_path`: (Optional) Path to musubi-tuner installation\n- `execute`: Set to True to start training\n\nWhen save state is set to true, a checkpoint of the training will be generated when we save a version as a save_state folder\nYou can resume a training by setting the path to that save_state folder\n\n**Outputs**:\n- `status`: Current status message\n- `log`: Detailed training log\n\n**Usage**: Connect dataset config and run training. Monitor the log output for progress.\n\n### 4. ❄️ ❄️ Musubi Image Viewer (Auto-Refresh)\n**Purpose**: Refreshes and displays new images in samples folder during training to monitor progress\n\n**Outputs**:\nLast training sample\n\n**Usage**: Setup before training to configure sampling. The node will automatically display the latest generated sample during training.\n\n\n## ⚙️ Advanced Features\n\n### High Noise Training (WAN 2.2)\nEnable `use_high_noise` and provide both low and high noise model paths for better quality results.\n\n### Preset Management\nThe nodes remember your last settings between sessions, making it easy to run multiple training jobs.\n\n### Real-time Monitoring\nThe Sampling node automatically refreshes to show your latest generated samples, giving you immediate feedback on training progress.\n\n## 🎛️ Training Parameters Guide\n\n### Learning Rate\n- **Default**: 0.0003\n- **Range**: 0.00001 - 0.01\n- Lower values = slower but more stable training\n- Higher values = faster but risk instability\n\n### Network Dim (LoRA Rank)\n- **Default**: 32\n- **Range**: 1 - 128\n- Higher = more expressive but slower\n- I like to start with 32, increase if needed\n\n### Network Alpha\n- **Default**: 32 (usually same as dim)\n- **Range**: 1 - 128\n- Controls LoRA weight scaling\n\n### Max Train Steps\n- **Default**: 2000 but can be done by 500\n- Depends on dataset size\n- More data = more steps needed\n- Monitor samples to avoid overtraining, stop when you get good enough likeness\n\n### Gradient Checkpointing\n- **Default**: True\n- Saves VRAM at cost of speed\n- Disable if you have plenty of VRAM\n\n### FP8 Base\n- **Default**: True\n- Uses FP8 precision for memory efficiency\n- Recommended for large models\n\n## 🐛 Troubleshooting\n\n### \"Dataset config not found\"\nMake sure the Dataset Config node executed successfully and check the output path.\n\n### \"VAE/T5/DiT path not found\"\nVerify all model paths are correct and files exist at those locations.\n\n### \"Caching failed\"\n- Check that dataset_config points to valid data\n- Ensure video/image files exist in specified directory\n- Verify caption files match your data files\n\n### \"Training failed\"\n- Ensure caching completed successfully first\n- Check that you have enough VRAM\n- Enable gradient checkpointing and FP8 if needed\n- Review the log output for specific errors\n\n### Sampling node not showing images\n- Make sure `folder_path` points to where samples are saved\n- Check that `auto_refresh` is enabled\n- Samples only appear after training generates them\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
